      "components": [
        {
          "id": "rtc_1M6NMG60MSBXQ6VN",
          "display_name": "Pyrolyzer CH₄ time emissions",
          "description": "CO emission rate from the pyrolyzer flue gas: 0.12487 ± 0.02792 kg CO₂e/h (±22.4%). Value: flue gas mass flow (5.25 t/h, from measured volumetric flow at 400 °C via the ideal gas law) × CO mass concentration (7.92841×10⁻³ kg/t, from 8.21 ppmv measured at the test point) × GWP₁₀₀ of CO (3.0, IPCC AR6 WGI Ch.7 SM) = 0.12487 kg CO₂e/h. Uncertainty: the relative uncertainties of the multiplied inputs are combined by root sum of squares. Mass flow ±20% (1.05 t/h), CO concentration ±10% (0.79284×10⁻³ kg/t), GWP 0% (fixed IPCC value). Relative uncertainty = √(0.20² + 0.10² + 0²) = 0.2236 (22.4%). Absolute uncertainty = 0.12487 × 0.2236 = 0.02792 kg CO₂e/h. Sources: [stack test report, date]; [LCA & Sensitivity Analysis DEC TZ001B, Assumptions rows 64, 67, 69]. Time duration Pyrolyzer operating hours over the project lifetime: 70,080 ± 14,016 h (±20%). Value: 10 years × 8,760 h/year × 80% operational uptime = 70,080 h. Uncertainty: the project lifetime (10 years) and hours per year (8,760) are fixed, so all uncertainty comes from the uptime estimate, which is ±20% (estimated over machinery lifetime). Absolute uncertainty = 70,080 × 0.20 = 14,016 h. Source: [LCA & Sensitivity Analysis DEC TZ001B, Assumptions rows 5, 8].",
          "blueprint_key": "time_based_emissions",
          "ghg_entry_template_id": "rvt_1KS4S43VPSBXA26X",
          "ghg_entry_template_component_group_id": "rtg_1KS4S43VPSBXCAH6",
          "inputs": [
